 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## **CHARTING A COURSE FOR MWANGAZA FILM STUDIO**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### **PROJECT OBJECTIVES**\n",
    "Help Mwangaza studio determine what kinds of movies are most successful at the box office, using available data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### **DATA**\n",
    "In the zippedData folder, movie datasets were sourced from Box Office Mojo, IMDb, Rotten Tomatoes, The Movie Database (TMDb), and The Numbers. Specifically, the files used were:\n",
    "\n",
    "tn.movie_budgets.csv:used for production budgets and release dates.\n",
    "\n",
    "bom.movie_gross.csv.gz: provided domestic and worldwide gross earnings.\n",
    "\n",
    "im.db.zip (from IMDb): included the movie_basics and movie_ratings tables for IMDb ratings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### **RESEARCH OBJECTIVES**\n",
    "- **Determine Market Viability – Assess which types of films resonate most with audiences and what factors contribute to commercial success.**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Guide Strategic Decision-Making – Provide recommendations on which genres, styles, or storytelling approaches the new company should pursue.**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **To determine the optimal range of movie runtime that is most often associated with high box office success and use it to give insights on the length of an ideal movie.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### LIBRARIES"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
